==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|bawlen|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|non}} {{term|baula||to low|lang=non}} and/or {{etyl|ML.}} {{term|baulo|baulō|bark|pos=verb|lang=la}}, both from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|bau-||to roar|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|bau-||to bark|lang=ine-pro}}, conflated with {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|bellaną|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|ballijaną|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|buljaną||to shout, low, roar|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|bʰel-||to sound, roar|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|baula||to moo, low|lang=is}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|böla||to bellow, low|lang=sv}}. More at {{l/en|bell}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|[bɔːɫ]}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/bɔl/}}
* {{a|cot-caught}} {{IPA|/bɑl/}}
* {{rhymes|ɔːl}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|ball}}<!--perhaps not in all dialects but in Australian English and in New York City-->

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{intransitive}} To [[shout]] or [[utter]] in a loud and [[intense]] manner.
# {{intransitive}} To [[wail]]; to give out a [[blaring]] [[cry]].

